\textbf{13.} Age structure:
considering the density of age at time $t$ leads to a PIDE.

\textbf{14.} Spatial structure.
Meta-population models consider patches, with travel between patches,
or with residents of patch $i$ spending a portion $p_{ij}$ of their time in patch $j$
(continuous distributions lead to PDEs: reaction-diffusion equations).

