  with Huber loss, and elastic net penalty
\item NLP: cryptocurrency related words in management presentations and conference calls.
\end{compactitem}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Text-based network industries\\ and endogenous product differentiation}\\
  G. Hoberg and G. Phillips (2009)
\end{book}
Take the product description from the 10K filings,
only keep nouns and proper nouns (they are capitalized 90\% of the time),
discard geographic words, and words appearing in more than 25\% of the documents;
compute pairwise cosine similarity
to get each company's neighbours.

Either use this weighted graph to compute a fixed industry classification
(apply some clustering algorithm on data from 1997)
or truncate the graph
(to have the same number of connected pairs as in the SIC-3 classification).

