  \emph{Evaluating the visualization\\ of what a deep neural network has learned}\\
  W. Samek et al.
\end{book}
\emph{Layerwise relevance propagation} (LRP) gives,
for each layer,
a decomposition of the network output
(e.g., the log-odds, for a classification problem)
into contributions of the individual neurons of that layer;
in particular, the sum of the contributions
is the same for all layers:
\[ \sum_i R_i^{(\ell)} = \sum_j R_j^{(\ell+1)}. \]
The contributions in layer $\ell$ can be computed from those in layer $\ell+1$,
for instance as
\begin{align*}
  R_i^{(\ell)} &= \sum_j \left(
  \alpha \dfrac{ z_{ij}^+ }{ \sum\limits_{i'} z_{i'j}^+ } +
  \beta  \dfrac{ z_{ij}^- }{ \sum\limits_{i'} z_{i'j}^- } +
  \right) R_j^{(\ell+1)} \\
  z_{ij} &= w_{ij} ^{( \ell \to \ell+1)} a_i^{(\ell)} \\
  z_{ij} &= z_{ij}^+ + z_{ij}^- \\
  \rlap{\ensuremath{\alpha+\beta=1.}}\hphantom{z_{ij}}
\end{align*}

