scRENseq data contains biological zeroes (no gene expression) an technical zeroes (``dropouts'').
Since
$Z_i \indep Z_j \iff X_i \indep X_j | R = 0$, we can just drop the zeroes (dropouts and biological zeroes)
and recover the correct conditional  independence relations.
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,xscale=.9,yscale=.9,inner sep=.5pt,outer sep=1pt,baseline=0]
  \node[circle,draw] (R) at (0,0) {$R$};
  \node[circle,draw] (X) at (1,0) {$X$};
  \node[circle,draw,densely dotted] (Z) at (0,1) {$Z$};
  \node[circle,draw,densely dotted] (D) at (1,1) {$D$};
  \draw[->] (Z) -- (R);
  \draw[->] (Z) -- (X);
  \draw[->] (D) -- (R);
  \draw[->] (D) -- (X);
  \draw[->] (Z) -- (D);
\end{tikzpicture}
\qquad
\begin{aligned}
  Z &:\  \text{True expression} \\
  D &:\  \mathbf 1_{\text{dropout}} \\
  X &:\  \text{observed expression} \\
  R &:\  \text{observed zero} \\
\end{aligned}
\]

