\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{ASID: active exploration\\ for system identification in robotic manipulation}\\
  M. Memmel et al. (2024)
\end{book}
Model-free RL is sample-inefficient,
but model-based RL requires an accurate world simulator:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Start with an inaccurate simulator (correct model, with approximate parameters);
\item Train an exploring agent, maximizing Fisher information
  \[ \operatorname*{Minimize}_\pi \operatorname{trace} I \bigl( p_{\theta^*} ( \cdot | \pi ) \bigr) \]
  (where $p$ is the distribution on trajectories);
\item Collect real-world data; 
\item Use it to refine the simulator; 
\item Train the (exploiting) agent.
\end{compactitem}

