\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Probabilistic machine learning}\\
  K.P. Murphy (2022)
\end{book}
% 1. Introduction
\textbf{1.}
A \emph{machine learning} problem combines a task, training data, and a performance measure.
\emph{Epistemic} uncertainty (model uncertainty) reflects our ignorance of the model.
\emph{Aleatoric} uncertainty (data uncertainty) reflects the noise in the model.

