\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Span-based joint entity and relation extraction with transformer pretraining}\\
  M. Eberts and A. Ulges (2021)
\end{book}
SpERT uses fine-tuned BERT embeddings to filter ans classify spans (NER)
and relations
\[ \llbracket i , i+k \rrbracket \longmapsto f( e_i , \dots , e_{i+k} ) \sqcup w_{k+1} \sqcup c \]
where
$\llbracket i , i+k \rrbracket$ is the candidate span,
$e_i,\dots,e_{i+k}$ are the token embeddings,
$k+1$ is the span length,
$w_{k+1}$ is a learned embedding of the span length,
$c$ is the embedding of the \textsc{cls} token (of the whole sentence),
$\sqcup$ is concatenation.

For relations, use the max-pooling of the spans and of the context.

