\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Agent market orders representation\\ through a contrastive learning approach}\\
  R. Ruan et al.
\end{book}
To cluster traders, \ie, identify trading behaviours,
consider sequences of 50 market orders by several traders,
and use an LSTM with contrastive learning (triplet loss,
with positive/negative pairs if the sequences come / do not come
from the same trader)
to learn a latent representations,
and use $k$-means on it.
Plot with $t$-SNE, or $\text{hour} \sim \text{date} \mid \text{cluster}$.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Causal feature engineering\\ of price directions of cryptocurrencies\\ using dynamic Bayesian networks}\\
  R. Amirzadeh et al.
\end{book}
DBN (dynamic Bayesian network) to predict the price direction of 5 altcoins
from 23 features (technical analysis, gold, MSCI, S\&P, USD, oil, number of tweets).

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Random matrix theory and nested clustered portfolios on Mexican markets}\\
  A. Garcia and B. Rodr\'iguez
\end{book}
Nested clustered optimization (NCO) for $n=28$:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Start with the variance matrix (sample, shrinkage, or cleaned with RMT);
\item Compute the corresponding minimum spanning tree,
  its normalized Laplacian $L$, and the spectrum of $L$;
\item Only keep the eigenvectors before the maximum spectral gap,
  $\max_k \va{ \lambda_k - \lambda_{k-1} }$;
\item Apply $k$-means on the top eigenvectors;
\item Compute the optimal portfolio inside each cluster;
\item Compute the optimal portfolio of clusters.
\end{compactitem}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Model-free market risk hedging\\ using crowding networks}\\
  V. Zlotnikov et al. (2023)
\end{book}
Crowding measures whether active managers are overweight a stock
(other measures include: proportion of buy ratings,
institutional trade persistence,
momentum,
high but achievable expectations).
It can be estimated with the centrality in the overweight (resp. underweight)
graph built from holdings data.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Causality between sentiment\\ and cryptocurrency prices}\\
  L. Mondal et al.
\end{book}
Fit a topic model on crypto-related tweets (a variant of LDA
targetted at shorter texts, only allowing one topic per text)
and compute topic-level sentiment
(BERTweet and Pysentimiento).
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Coloring in R's blind spot}\\
  A. Zeileis and P. Murrell
\end{book}
R 4.0.0 provides qualitative palettes in \texttt{palette.\break colors} and
sequential and diverging ones in \texttt{hcl.colors}.

