\end{tikzpicture}
\!\!\!\right)
\]
\end{compactitem}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Industry classification using a novel financial time series case representation}\\
  R. Dolphin et al.
\end{book}
Compute an embedding of stocks from pricing data:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item $S_{ij} = {}$similarity between the delay embeddings ($\tau=5$)
  of the daily return time series
\item $C_{ij}={}$number of times stock $i$ is among the $k$ nearest neighbours of stock $j$
  ($k=1$);
\item $C \approx E E'$, low-rank factorization, ignoring the diagonal
  (after log-transforming the entries of $C$).
\end{compactitem}
Visualize the truncated graph with t-SNE.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Hedonic prices and\\ quality-adjusted price indices powered by AI}\\
  P. Bajari et al. (2023)
\end{book}
Forecast product prices from (time-stamped) unstructured product data
(text, image: BERT and ResNet50)
and use this model to measure \emph{inflation}.
\begin{align*}
  \text{Price}_{it} &= h_t( \text{features}_{it} ) + \epsilon_{it} \\
  \text{or } \text{Price}_{i,\bigcdot} &= h(\text{features}_i) + \epsilon_{i,\bigcdot}
\end{align*}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Precision versus shrinkage:\\ a comparative analysis of covariance estimation methods for portfolio allocation}\\
  S. Dutta and J. Jain (2023)
\end{book}
To estimate the variance matrix, for portfolio optimization, prefer Gaussian graphical models:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Graphical lasso
  \[ \operatorname*{Minimize}_{ \Theta \succcurlyeq 0 }
  \log \det \Theta - \tr ( \hat \Sigma \Theta ) - \lambda \n \Theta _1 \]
\item Nodewise regression;
\item Clime
  \[ \operatorname*{Minimize}_{\Theta \succcurlyeq 0} \n \Theta _1
  \text{ such that } \n{ \hat \Sigma \Theta - I }_\infty \leq \lambda \]
\item Greedy prune:
  find the neighbours of $i$ by adding the variable $X_j$ minimizing
  $ \var[ X_1 | X_{ \mathscr N(i) } , X_j ] $,
  $T$ times, and then pruning those contributing to a proportion less than $\nu$ to the variance;
\item Hybrid MB: nodewise regression with no $L^1$ penalty on the nearest neighbour,
  followed by pruning.
\end{compactitem}

Alternatives include
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Linear shrinkage (for various choices of the target and the shrinkage constant:
  Ledoit-Wolf,
  Rao-Blackwell-Ledoit-Wolf,
  Bodnar,
  oracle);
\item Non-linear shrinkage (shrink the eigenvalues of $\hat \Sigma$ separately,
  to minimize some loss function);
\item Thresholding (of the covariances): hard, soft, or adaptive;
\item Random matrix theory (rotationally invariant estimators).
\end{compactitem}
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Non-parametric cumulants approach for outlier detection of multivariate financial data}\\
  F. Cesarone et al. (2023)
\end{book}
The CGF-PCA (cumulant generating function) direction is the solution $\theta$ of
\[ \operatorname*{Maximize}_{ \theta \ :\ \n \theta = 1 } \log \E[ e^{ r \theta' X } ] \]
for a fixed $r>0$.
We are maximizing (not minimizing) a convex function on the sphere (a non-convex set) --
but we can replace $\n \theta = 1$ with $\n \theta \leq 1$
and solve with multistart and projected gradient.

Identify outliers by looking at the projection onto $\operatorname{Span} \theta$.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Multivariate range value-at-risk and covariance risk measures for elliptical and log-elliptical distributions}\\
  B. Zuo et al.
\end{book}
The multivariate range VaR is
\[ \E[ X \,|\, \forall i \ \text{VaR}_{p_i} X_i \leq X_i \leq \text{VaR}_{q_i} X_i ]. \]
The multivariate range covariance is
\begin{align*}
  & \E\bigl[
  ( X - \text{MRVaR}_{pq} ) ( X - \text{MRVaR}_{pq} )'
    \,| \\
  & \hspace*{4cm}
  \text{VaR}_p X \leq X \leq \text{VaR}_q X 
  \bigr]. 
\end{align*}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Market making with deep reinforcement learning from limit order books}\\
  H. Guo et al.
\end{book}
% clear
The state space contains the current LOB (limit order book:
price,  volume, ask, bid, several levels),
order imbalance (several windows), realized volatility, technical indicators,
inventory, remaining time.
Try to forecast the price direction $[t-k,t]$ vs $[t,t+k]$.
The reward includes a damped PnL
\[ (1-\lambda) ( \Delta \text{PnL} )_+ - ( \Delta \text{PnL} )_- \]
and an inventory penalty.
Train with Dueling DQN or PPO.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Trending fast and slow}\\
  E. Cheng et al.
\end{book}
Trend following strategies with a volatility dependent lookback (1m vs 12m):
slow momentum in low volatility and fast momentum in high volatility work better.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{LLaMa: open and efficient\\ foundation language models}\\
  H. Touvron et al. (2023)
\end{book}
LLaMa is a family of large language models (LLM),
from 13B to 5B parameters,
designed to be inexpensive at inference time,
trained using only publically available data:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item CommonCrawl/C4, preprocessed in different ways
  (deduplication, quality filtering, identification of
  Wikipedia references);
\item Github (BigQuery, filtered for free licences,
  deduplicated, with boilerplate removal);
\item Wikipedia (20 languages, boilerplate removed);
\item Arxiv (\LaTeX\ files, staring at the first section and ending
  before the references, with macros removed;
\item StackExchange (without HTML, with answers sorted by score);
\item Gutenberg and Books3 (deduplicated);
\end{compactitem}
using
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Byte pair encoding (BPE, SentencePiece);
\item Prenormaliztion (normalize the input of the transformers, instead of the output, as GPT3);
\item SwiGLU (as PaLM);
\begin{align*}
  \text{GLU}(a,b) &= a \odot \sigma(b) \\
  \text{Swish}_\beta(x) &= x \odot \sigma(\beta x) =
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,scale=.3,inner sep=2pt,outer sep=0pt,baseline=0]
  \draw[thick,blue!70!black]
