\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Improving causal discovery\\ by optimal Bayesian network learning}\\
  N.Y. Lu et al. (2021)
\end{book}
Triplet $A^*$ speeds up $A^*$-based causal discovery
by restricting the search for $\text{Pa}(x)$ to subsets of neighbours of
$y$---$x$---$z$ (given a PC-based initial guess of parents and children of each node).
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Domain-knowledge\\ in $A^*$-based causal discovery}\\
  S. Kleinegesse et al.
\end{book}
Add domain knowledge ($x \in \text{Pa}(y)$ or $x \not\in \text{Pa}(y)$)
to $A^*$ score-based causal discovery.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Reliable causal discovery\\ with improved exact search\\ and weaker assumptions}\\
  I. Ng et al. (2021)
\end{book}
Speed up $A^*$-based causal discovery
by limiting the size of the parent graphs
($A^*$ superstructure) and/or limiting the seach to the 2-hop neighbourhood
of each variable in its graphical lasso graph (local $A^*$).
  
