all have 3 coordinates: lightness, red-green, yellow-blue.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Nonparametric Bayesian deep networks\\ with local competition}\\
  K.P. Panousis et al. (2019)
\end{book}
To automatically prune a neural network,
use a Bayesian neural net,
with latent Bernoulli variables indicating which weights should be kept, following an
Indian buffet process (IBP)
\[
<<IBP202304,results='hide',echo=FALSE,fig.width=4.5,fig.height=1.5,out.width='\\hsize',fig.show='hold'>>=
n <- 30
m <- 100
alpha <- 50
u <- rbeta(m, alpha, 1)
p <- cumprod(u)
z <- matrix( runif(n*m), m, n )
z <- ifelse( z <= p, 1, 0 )
op <- par( mar = c(0,0,0,0) + .1 )
image(z, axes=FALSE)
par(op)
@
\]
\vspace*{-7mm}
\begin{align*}
  u_k &\sim \text{Beta}(\alpha, 1) \\
  \pi_k &\sim \prod_{ 1 \leq i \leq k } u_i \\
  z_{ik} &\sim \text{Bernoulli}( \pi_k )
\end{align*}
  
