\begin{book}
  \emph{Addendum on how many times\\ cointelated pairs cross paths}\\
  B. Mahdavi-Damghani and S. Roberts (2020)
\end{book}
The \emph{cointelation} model allows for arbitrary short-term correlation
(even $\rho=-1$) and mean reversion ($\rho=+1$ in the long term).
\begin{align*}
  \dfrac{ dX }{ X } &= \mu dt + \sigma d W_1 && \text{leading} \\
  dY &= \theta( X-Y) dt + \sigma Y dW_2 &&\text{lagging} \\
  d\langle W_i , W_2 \rangle &= \rho dt
\end{align*}
  
