\end{book}
Simple randomization can lead to accidental bias. Try:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Block randomization;
\item Stratified randomization
\item Minimization: allocate the new subject (with high probability, e.g., $p=0.8$)
  to produce the smallest total imbalance (variance, standard deviation, range, etc.)
  over its baseline characteristics; 
\item Dynamic hierarchical randomization: idem, after putting the baseline characteristics in a tree.
\end{compactitem}
  
