Nonnegative matrix factorization (NMF) is asymmetric: it pays more attention to high values than low values.
Instead, decompose the data as $X = X_0 + X_+ - X_-$, $X_+ \geq 0$, $X_- \geq 0$, for some baseline $X_0$
(e.g., the column-wise medians) and use a nonnegative \emph{tensor} factorization
for the order-3 tensor $[ X_+ | X_- ]$.

