  R. Ying et al. (2019)
\end{book}
To explain the output of a GNN, for a given input,
look for a small subgraph, and a subset of features, such that altering those features on that subgraph significantly changes the output -- mutual information $H(Y) - H(Y|S)$ measures that.
  
