\begin{book}
  \emph{Gamma and vega hedging using\\ deep distributional reinforcement learning}\\
  J. Cao et al. (2022)
\end{book}
Assuming that $\Delta$-hedging (of an option portfolio) can be done without cost,
use D3PG to learn a gamma and vega hedging strategy using options,
where the state is
(asset price, portfolio gamma, portfolio vega),
the action is the number of options to hold,
and the reward is
\[ \text{change in portfolio value} - \text{option cost}. \]
 
