  T.D. Sim\~ao et al. (2021)
\end{book}
\emph{Factored} constrained Markov decision processes (CMDP)
use a small subset of the features to describe the dynamics relevant to the safety constraints:
the safety dynamics are easier to learn,
and the model can be deployed, safely, to continue learning.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Constrained optimal stopping time\\ under a regime-switching model}\\
  T. Arai and M. Takenaka (2022)
\end{book}
The optimal stopping time
\begin{align*}
  & \operatorname*{Argmax}_\tau \E \bigl[ e^{ - r \tau } \pi( X_\tau ) \bigm| X_0 = x \bigr] \\
  & \pi(x) = \E \Bigl[ \int_t^\infty e^{ -r ( t - s ) } X_s ds - I \Bigm| X_t = x \Bigr]
\end{align*}
is sometimes of \emph{threshold type}
\[ \tau^* = \inf \{ t > 0 \ :\ X_t \geq x^* \} \]
($X_t$ is a regime switching geometric Brownian motion,
and the stopping time is constrained to exogenous random times (Poisson) and regime 1).
  
