\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Landscape of academic finance\\ with the structural topic model}\\
  D. Ardia et al. (2022)
\end{book}
The \emph{structural topic model} (STM) extends the latent Dirichlet allocation (LDA)
and correlated topic models (CTM)
by allowing for document covariates (e.g., time).
\begin{align*}
  d &\text{: document} \\
  k &\text{: topic} \\
  n &\text{: word} \\
  X_d &\text{: covariates} \\
  \theta_d&\text{: distribution of topics in document $d$} \\
  \theta_d | X_d &\sim \text{LogisticNormal} \\
  \beta_k &\text{: distribution of words in topic $k$} \\
  \beta_k &\propto \exp ( m + \kappa_k ) \\
  z_{d,n} | \theta_d & \sim \text{Multinomial} \qquad \text{topic of word $n$} \\
  w_{d,n} | \beta_{z_{d,n}} & \sim \text{Multinomial} \qquad \text{word $n$}  
\end{align*}
  
