  S.L. Smith et al. (2021)
\end{book}
Full-batch gradient descent with \emph{finite} step size can be described as a modified gradient flow,
with a regularizer $\tfrac14\alpha\n{\nabla \ell}^2$,
where $\alpha$ is the learning rate.
For SGD, the implicit regularization is
\[ \dfrac{\alpha}{4m} \sum \n{ \nabla \ell_i }^2. \]

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Implicit gradient regularization}\\
  D.G.T. Barrett and B. Dherin (2021)
\end{book}
The \emph{discrete} steps of gradient descent lead the model away from the steepest descent path on the loss landscape. This path can be described as the steepest descent path on a modified loss landscape.
The modified loss uses a gradient penalty
$\dfrac\alpha4\sum\n{\nabla\ell_i}^2$.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{The implicit regularization\\ of stochastic gradient flow for least squares}\\
  A. Ali et al. (2020)
\end{book}
Gradient descent for least squares
\[ \operatorname*{Minimize} _\beta \dfrac1{2n} \n{ y - X \beta }^2 \]
with infinitesimal step sizes is described by the \emph{gradient flow}
\[ \dot \beta_t = \dfrac1n X' ( y - X \beta_t ), \quad \beta_0=0. \]
Stochastic gradient descent,
with minibatches $I$ of size $\va I = m$, can be described by a SDE
\begin{align*}
  d\beta &= \dfrac1n X'(y-X\beta) dt + \epsilon Q(\beta)^{1/2} dW \\
  Q(\beta) &= \cov_I \left[ \dfrac1m X_I' (y_I - X_I \beta ) \right].
\end{align*}
It is similar to ridge regression with $\lambda = 1/t$.

\nextbook
