Two nodes are \d{$d$-separated} if all paths between them are blocked;
$d$-separation implies conditional independence (global Markov property).
\[
X \indep_{\!\!G}\, Y \,|\, Z
\ \implies \
X \indep_{\!\!P}\, Y \,|\, Z
\]

% Confounding vs causal associations
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,xscale=.8,yscale=.8,inner sep=1pt,outer sep=0pt,baseline=0, text width=1em,
    every node/.style={circle,draw},
  every text node part/.style={align=center}
