\]

To compute the signature: \texttt{signatory} (Python).

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Fractional SDE-Net: generation\\ of time series data with long-term memory}\\
  K. Hayashi and K. Nakagawa (2022)
\end{book}
Neural ODEs can be generalized to neural SDEs (by adding noise)
and neural fractional SDEs (if $H \neq \tfrac12$, It\=o calculus no longer applies
but, for $H>\tfrac12$, we can still define a stochastic integral).

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Holdout-based fidelity and privacy assessment of mixed-type synthetic data}\\
  M. Platzer and T. Reutterer
\end{book}
To measure fidelity and privacy risk of generated data,
look at:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item 1- and 2-dimensional distributions;
\item The distance to the closest observation in the training data
\end{compactitem}
and compare them with the holdout set.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Multi-asset spot and option market simulation}\\
  M. Wiese et al.
\end{book}
Generate synthetic time series with normalizing flows
\[ \begin{array}{rcl}
  (\mathscr F_t , Z_{t+1} ) & \longmapsto & X_{t+1} \\
  Z_{t+1} & \mathrel{\reflectbox{\ensuremath{\longmapsto}}} & ( \mathscr F_t , X_{t+1} )
\end{array} \]
where $X$ is observed, $Z$ latent,
and $\mathscr F_t = (X_t, X_{t-1}, \dots)$.
For option prices, enforcing the no-arbitrage condition complicates things.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{A hybrid deep learning approach to\\ purchasing strategy of carbon emission rights}\\
  J. Xu and Y. Fu 
\end{book}
Stack GARCH and GRU to forecast carbon emission prices.
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,xscale=1.7,yscale=.4,inner sep=0pt,outer sep=1pt,baseline=0,
  %every node/.style={circle,draw},
