  M.F. Dixon and I. Halperin (2020)
\end{book}
\emph{G-learning} is Q-learning (off-policy RL)
with an entropy penalty $H(\pi)$ or $\text{KL}(\pi\|\pi_0)$.
The \emph{free energy} $F$ is the entropy-regularized state value funtction.
The \emph{$G$-function} is the entropy-regularized state-action value function.

With a few (Gaussian) assumptions and (quadratic) approximations,
the problem is tractable.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{AlphaPortfolio: direct construction\\ through deep reinforcement learning\\ and interpretable AI}\\\
  L.W. Cong (2019)
\end{book}
% Well-written; presentation at the LQG
Train a neural network, computing portfolio weights, from 12 months of 50 features
(price, investments, profitability, intangibles, value, liquidity)
for 3000 stocks, over 50 years, on 2-year mini-batches, to directly minimize the information ratio.
One can add interactions with the environment:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Trading costs;
\item Trade impact;
\item Fund failure (loss beyond 50\% within 1 year).
\end{compactitem}
The portfolio is $Q$ stocks long, $Q$ stocks short, with exponentially decaying weights.

The network could be an LSTM with attention
\begin{align*}
  h_k &= \text{LSTM}( h_{k-1}, x_k ) \\
  r &= \sum_k \textsc{ATT}( h_K, h_k ) h_k \\
  \textsc{ATT}(h_K, h_k) &= \dfrac{ \exp \alpha_k }{ \displaystyle\sum\limits_\ell \exp \alpha_\ell } \\
  \alpha_k &= W_0 ' \tanh ( W_1 h_k + W_2 h_K )
\end{align*}
or a transformer (concatenation of several attention blocks)
\begin{align*}
  V, K, Q &= W_0 x, W_1 x, W_2 x \\
  \text{Attention}(Q,K,V) &= \text{Softmax} \left( \dfrac{ Q K' }{ \sqrt{ d_k } } \right) V
\end{align*}
(here, $\sqrt {d_k}$ helps keep the variance around 1).

Each asset is processed separately,
and the results are combined with a \emph{cross-asset attention network} (CAAN)
\begin{align*}
  q_i, k_i, v_i &= W_Q r_i, W_K r_i, W_V r_i \\
  \beta_{ij} &= \dfrac{ q_i ' k_j }{ \sqrt{ d_k } } \\
  a_i &= \sum_j \textsc{SATT} ( q_i , k_j ) v_j \\
  \textsc{SATT} ( q_i , k_j ) &= \dfrac{ \exp \beta_{ij} }{ \displaystyle\sum_\ell \exp \beta_{i\ell} } \\
  s_i &= \tanh( w' a_i + e ).
\end{align*}
To interpret the model:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Take the features with the largest
  $ \E \left[ \va{\dfrac{\partial \text{IR}(x) }{ \partial x_i }  } \right]$
  and use them in a polynomial regression with a lasso penalty;
\item Alternatively, use ``textual factors'' (topics)
  from SEC filings to reproduce (distill) the model outputs.
\end{compactitem}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Multi-horizon forecasting\\ for limit order books:\\ novel deep learning approaches\\ and hardware acceleration\\ using intelligent processing units}\\
  Z. Zhang and S. Zohren (2021)
\end{book}
Sequence-to-sequence (seq2seq) model, with attention, for multi-step forecasts of price changes
(direction or value) from limit order book (LOB) data).
Process the LOB (bid, ask, volume, price) as if it were an image, with inception modules.
\begin{align*}
  &\text{input} & x_t \\
  &\text{encoder} & h_i &= f(h_{i-1},x_i) \\
  &\text{context} & c_t &= \sum_i \alpha_{it} h_i \\
  &\text{decoder} & h'_t &= f( h'_{t-1} , t_{t-1} , c_t ) \\
  &\text{output} & y_t &\sim g( h'_t , c_t ) \\
  &\text{attention weights} & \alpha_{it} &\propto \exp h_i ^\top h'_{t-1} \\
  &&&\text{or } \exp h_i ^\top W h'_{t-1} \\
  &&&\text{or } \exp \tanh W [ h_i ; h'_{t-1} ] \\
  && i&: \text{ time (past)} \\
  && t&: \text{ time (future)}
\end{align*}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Textual factors: a scalable, interpretable,\\ and data-friven approach\\ to analyzing unstructured information}\\
  L.W. Cong et al. (2018)
\end{book}
Combine word embeddings and topic models:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Compute word2vec embeddings
\item Group the words into clusters, using LSH (locality-sensitive hashing);
\item Assume that the topics are the clusters, and estimate a topic model, one topic at a time.
\end{compactitem}
Applications:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Macroeconomic (CPI, GDP, housing prices, unemployment, S\&P, investment)
  forecasts from news (WSJ);
\item VIX back-filling (1889 to 1986);
\item Model interpretation.
\end{compactitem}

