\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Principal component-guided sparse regression}\\
  J.K. Tay et al (2018)
\end{book}
Ridge regression (and elastic net) slightly bias the solution towards the leading singular
vectors of $X$. \d{PClasso} provides a more aggressive shrinkage by replacing the ridge
penalty $\beta' \beta$ with $\beta' V Z V' \beta$
where $X = U D V'$ is the SVD and $Z = \operatorname{diag}( d_1^2 - d_k^2 )_{1\leq k \leq m}$.

If the factors are known to form groups, treat each separately.

The contours of the pclasso penalty are $\ell^1$ balls
more or less elongated in the direction of the first singular vectors.
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Efficient scalable algorithms\\ for hierarchically semiseparable matrices}\\
  S. Wang et al.
\end{book}
HSS matrices are block matrices, with dense diagonal blocks and low-rank off-diagonal blocks.

