\]
and aggregate measures of dependence (Kendall's $\tau$) or tail dependence
(tail dependence coefficient $\lambda$) as
\[ \dfrac{ \va{ \tau_{j,k} } }{ \sum\limits_{ \{j,k\} \subset i } \va{ \tau_i } }. \]

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Market making via reinforcement learning}\\
  T. Spooner et al. (2018)
\end{book}
Define the reward as P\&L penalized against speculation (inventory$\times$change in price).
For the state, use the inventory, the spread, the price change, the book imbalance,
the signed volume, the volatility, and the RSI,
with \emph{tile coding} -- combine several discretizations of the state space,
e.g., from grids with different offsets.
Use TD (SARSA) with eligibility traces; train on market data.
The actions are
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,yscale=.1,xscale=.15,inner sep = 2pt, outer sep = 0pt,baseline=-7]
  \draw (-4,0) -- (4,0);
  \draw (-3,0) -- (-3,1);
  \draw (-2,0) -- (-2,1);
  \draw (-1,0) -- (-1,1);
  \draw (3,0)  -- (3,1);
  \draw (2,0)  -- (2,1);
  \draw (1,0)  -- (1,1);
  \draw[ultra thick] (-1,0) -- (-1,4);
  \draw[ultra thick] (1,0) -- (1,4);
\end{tikzpicture}
