\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Parametrized response zero-intelligence (PRZI) traders}\\
  D. Cliff (2021)
\end{book}
In the \emph{zero-intelligence constrained} (\textsc{zic}) strategy,
each trader has a side (buy or sell),
a limit price $\lambda$, only trades one share,
and samples their bid or ask uniformly in
$[p_{\text{min}},\lambda]$ or $[\lambda, p_{\text{max}}]$.

The \textsc{shvr} strategy bids one tick above the current best bid (if below $\lambda$).

The \textsc{gvwy} strategy bids at the trader's limit price (no profit, unless the trade crosses the spread).

Those strategies can be blended.

<<PRZI,results='hide',echo=FALSE,fig.width=5,fig.height=1.5,out.width='\\hsize',fig.show='hold'>>=
a <- .3
x1 <- seq(0,1,length=20)
ys1 <- list( x1^2, x1, sqrt(x1), 0*x1+1 )
x2 <- seq(a,1,length=20)
x3 <- 1 - (x2-a) / (1-a)
ys2 <- list( 0*x2+1, sqrt(x3), x3, x3^2 )
op <- par( mfrow=c(2,5), mar = .5 + c(0,0,0,0) )
try( plot( 1, 1, type = "h", lwd = 3, col='darkblue', xlim = c(0,1), ylim = c(0,1), axes = FALSE ) )
abline(h=0)
#box()
for( y in ys1 ) {
  try( plot( x1, y, type = "l", lwd = 3, col='darkblue', xlim = c(0,1), ylim = c(0,1), axes = FALSE ) )
  polygon( c(x1[1],x1,1), c(0,y,0), border=NA, col='lightblue' )
  lines( x1, y, lwd = 3, col='darkblue')
  abline(h=0)
  #box()
}
for( y in ys2 ) {
  try( plot( x2, y, type = "l", lwd = 3, col='darkblue', xlim = c(0,1), ylim = c(0,1), axes = FALSE ) )
  polygon( c(x2[1],x2,1), c(0,y,0), border=NA, col='lightblue' )
  lines( x2, y, lwd = 3, col='darkblue')
  abline(h=0)
  #box()
}
try( plot( a, 1, type = "h", lwd = 3, col='darkblue', xlim = c(0,1), ylim = c(0,1), axes = FALSE ) )
abline(h=0)
#box()
par(op)
@

