The AA (adaptive aggressiveness) strategy tunes its aggressivity
(eager to trade, even for lower profits, vs eager to profit, even for a lower probability of trade).
Prior algorithms include:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item \textsc{zip} (zero-intelligence plus), a variant of \textsc{zic}
  which progressively updates its profit margin;
\item \textsc{gd}, which estimates the probability that a bid will be accepted;
\item \textsc{gdx}, which also uses dynamic programming, and may delay trading,
  waiting for better market conditions.
\end{compactitem}
