\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{NAOMI: Non-autoregressive multiresolution sequence imputation}\\
  Y. Liu et al. (2019)
\end{book}
Deep generative models for sequences are autoregressive: errors compound.
Instead, use a multi-resolution approach:
feed the time series (with the missing values zeroed out)
and the mask to a BiLSTM,
predict $x_{n/2}$ from $h_0$ and $h_n$,
feed that new value to the network, and proceed recursively.
  
