There is a difference between stock characteristics (e.g., momentum)
and stock exposures (e.g., beta to a momentum portfolio):
only the former explain returns -- using the latter to adjust returns
(residuals of a regression against the factor portfolio)
is a bad idea.
  
\nextbook
