  S. Mussard and V. Terraza (2008)
\end{book}
The variance of a portfolio is
$w' V w = \sum w_i \sigma_i^2 + 2 \sum_{i<j} w_i w_j \rho_{ij} \sigma_i \sigma_j$;
the second term, the ``between security risk'',
can be decomposed into individual asset contributions with Shapley values.
  
