The Shapley decomposition of a variance game is
\[ \var\Bigl[ \sum X_i\Bigr ] = \sum_i \cov\biggl( X_i , \sum_j X_j \biggr). \]
  
\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{The Shapley value decomposition \\of optimal portfolios}\\
  H. Shalit (2017)
\end{book}
Use Shapley values to decompose the risk (volatility)
of the mean-variance and the \emph{mean-Gini} portfolio built on a set of assets.

The \emph{Gini mean difference} is
\[ \text{GMD}(X) = \tfrac12 \E_{X_1,X_2} \va{ X_1 - X_2 } = 2 \cov\bigl( X, F_X(X) \bigr). \]
  
