The \emph{conditional drawdown} (or conditional drawdown at risk,
or conditional expected drawdown)
is the average of the worst $\alpha$\% drawdowns.
Average and maximum drawdowns are special cases ($\alpha=1$ or $0$).
For portfolio optimization, assume the portfolio weights are constant
and consider ``uncompounded'' returns (\ie, assume that log- and ratio-returns are the same).

