  \emph{Learning to see through observations}\\
  Y.L. Liv et al (2020)
\end{book}
Remove window reflections or fence obstructions from short videos
using the motion difference between the obstrucion and the background.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Modeling 3D shapes by reinforcement learning}\\
  C. Lin et al.
\end{book}
Generate 3D shapes, as humans do in 3D software, in two steps:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item First, approximate the shape with 3D primitives;
\item Them, edit the mesh (edge loops rather than vertices) for the details.
\end{compactitem}
Use imitation learning of a heuristic policy as pretraining
before actual reinforcement learning.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Stanza: a Python NLP toolkit\\ for many human languages}\\
  P. Qi et al. (2020)
\end{book}
If CoreNLP, Flair, Spacy, UDpipe do not cover enough languages
(includes Japanese, Chinese, Arabic, but also ancient Greek, old French, etc. --
much fewer for NER).

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Deep rank-based transposition invariant distances on musical sequences}\\
  G. Hadjeres and F. Nielsen
\end{book}
To compute a distance between musical sequences,
train a seq2seq autoencoder
(or a seq2seq network to transpose motifs)
and use a permutation-based distance
(rank correlation or Kendall's $\tau$) on the high-level features (only use the $\ell$ largest features).

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{QuantGAN:\\ deep generation of financial time series}\\
  M. Wiese et al. (2019)
\end{book}
GAN, with a TCN in the generator, to model volatility, drift and innovations separately and reproduce the stylized facts of time series
(fat tails, clustered volatility, leverage $\cor(r,\sigma)<0$).
\[
(\eta_t)_t \longmapsto
(\sigma_t, \mu_t, \epsilon_t )_t \longmapsto
( \mu_t + \sigma_t \cdot \epsilon_t )_t
\]

