\]
or by caching the activations (WaveNet, fastPixelCCNN).

There is no straightforward latent representation (everything is pixelwise),
but the \emph{Fisher score}
\[ \dot \ell ( x , \theta ) = \nabla_{\!\theta} \log p_\theta(x) \]
can be used.
It also allows interpolation. % HOW?

\textbf{3.} \d{Flow models} allow sampling
$x \sim p_\theta$, probability computation $p_\theta(x)$
and also provide a latent representation.
They transform the input into a target distribution,
$z \sim p_z$, e.g., $z \sim N(0,1)$.
\[
x
\longrightarrow
\fbox{\vrule width 0pt height 1em depth 1ex} \to
\fbox{\vrule width 0pt height 1em depth 1ex} \to
\fbox{\vrule width 0pt height 1em depth 1ex}
\longrightarrow
a = f_\theta(x)
\]

In dimension 1, the distribution of $x$ is given by a change of variable,
provided $f_\theta$ is \emph{invertible},
\[ p_\theta(x) = p_z \bigl( f_\theta(x) \bigr) \va{ \dfrac{ \partial f_\theta(x) }{ \partial x } } \]
and $\theta$ can be found by maximizing
\[
\sum_i \log p_\theta(x_i) = \sum_i \log p_z\bigl( f_\theta(x_i) \bigr) +
\log \va{  \dfrac{ \partial f_\theta(x) }{ \partial x } (x_i) }.
\]

Sampling is straightforward: $z \sim p_z$, $x = f_\theta^{-1}(z)$.

In dimension 1, with $p_z = U(0,1)$, the flow is just the cdf of $x$,
and could be estimated as a mixture of Gaussians.
\[
\underset{\text{\footnotesize data}}{%
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,xscale=.3, yscale=1.8,inner sep=1pt, outer sep=1pt,baseline=10pt]
\draw[thick]
(-2.5,0.006)--(-2.45,0.008)--(-2.4,0.011)--(-2.35,0.015)--(-2.3,0.019)--(-2.25,0.025)--(-2.2,0.031)--(-2.15,0.04)--(-2.1,0.05)--(-2.05,0.062)--(-2,0.076)--(-1.95,0.092)--(-1.9,0.111)--(-1.85,0.132)--(-1.8,0.155)--(-1.75,0.181)--(-1.7,0.21)--(-1.65,0.24)--(-1.6,0.272)--(-1.55,0.305)--(-1.5,0.339)--(-1.45,0.373)--(-1.4,0.406)--(-1.35,0.437)--(-1.3,0.467)--(-1.25,0.493)--(-1.2,0.516)--(-1.15,0.534)--(-1.1,0.547)--(-1.05,0.556)--(-1,0.559)--(-0.95,0.556)--(-0.9,0.548)--(-0.85,0.534)--(-0.8,0.516)--(-0.75,0.493)--(-0.7,0.467)--(-0.65,0.438)--(-0.6,0.407)--(-0.55,0.374)--(-0.5,0.341)--(-0.45,0.309)--(-0.4,0.277)--(-0.35,0.246)--(-0.3,0.218)--(-0.25,0.192)--(-0.2,0.169)--(-0.15,0.149)--(-0.1,0.132)--(-0.05,0.118)--(0,0.108)--(0.05,0.101)--(0.1,0.097)--(0.15,0.096)--(0.2,0.098)--(0.25,0.102)--(0.3,0.109)--(0.35,0.117)--(0.4,0.128)--(0.45,0.139)--(0.5,0.151)--(0.55,0.164)--(0.6,0.177)--(0.65,0.19)--(0.7,0.202)--(0.75,0.212)--(0.8,0.222)--(0.85,0.229)--(0.9,0.235)--(0.95,0.238)--(1,0.24)--(1.05,0.238)--(1.1,0.235)--(1.15,0.229)--(1.2,0.221)--(1.25,0.211)--(1.3,0.2)--(1.35,0.187)--(1.4,0.174)--(1.45,0.16)--(1.5,0.145)--(1.55,0.131)--(1.6,0.117)--(1.65,0.103)--(1.7,0.09)--(1.75,0.078)--(1.8,0.067)--(1.85,0.056)--(1.9,0.047)--(1.95,0.039)--(2,0.032)--(2.05,0.026)--(2.1,0.021)--(2.15,0.017)--(2.2,0.013)--(2.25,0.011)--(2.3,0.008)--(2.35,0.006)--(2.4,0.005)--(2.45,0.004)--(2.5,0.003);
\draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (3,0);
