\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Dropout as a Bayesian approximation:\\ representing model uncertainty\\ in deep learning}\\
  Y. Gal an Z. Gharhamani (2015)
\end{book}
Dropout performs approximate Bayesian inference.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{High-dimensional Bayesian optimization using low-dimensional feature spaces}\\
  R. Moriconi et al.
  (NeurIPS 2019)
\end{book}
Bayesian optimization in high dimension ($d\geq20$) can use a random projection,
an additive decomposition of the objective function, or a nonlinear embedding, learned with a VAE, progressively, during optimization.
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,xscale=1,yscale=1,inner sep=0pt, outer sep=0pt, baseline=0]
  \node (X1) at (0,1) {$\mathscr X$};
