\]

%% NeurIPS workshop: Perception as generative reasoning

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Perception as generative reasoning:\\ structure, causality probability}\\
  (NeurIPS 2019)
\end{book}

\begin{align*}
  &\text{Discriminative model} && p(\text{label} | \text{image}) \\
  &\text{Generative model} && p(\text{image} | \text{label}) \times p(\text{label}) \\
\end{align*}

In the generative model, the first factor can include physics engines and renderers,
the second can add structure, e.g.,
$p(\text{label}) = p(\text{label}|z) p(z)$.

