Assume the transaction-cost-aware portfolio $x_t$
and the ideal portfolio (TC=0) $y_t$ are the hidden and observed states of a hidden Markov chain (HMM)
with transition and emission probabilities
\begin{align*}
  - \log p(x_t | x_{t-1} ) &= c_t(x_{t-1}, x_t) \\
  - \log p(p_t | x_t) &= \tfrac12 \lambda ( y_t - x_t) ' \Sigma (y_t - x_t).
\end{align*}
Treat one asset at a time, in a Gibbs fashion, until convergence (blockwise coordinate descent).

For time, either treat the periods one at a time, or use a particle filter.

