\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Neural architecture search with\\ Bayesian optimization and optimal transport} \\
  K. Kandasamy et al. (2018)
\end{book}
Gaussian-process-based Bayesian optimization can be used for network architecture search,
with optimal transport to define a kernel to compare architectures 
(align the two networks and add penalties for mismatches)
and an evolutionary algorithm to optimize the acquisition function.

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Neural architecture search: a survey} \\
  T. Elsken et al. (2018)
\end{book}

