\d{Vertex bootstrap} resamples the vertices of a graph, with replacement, 
and returns a new adjacency matrix;
for duplicated vertices, since there are no self-edges, take a random element of the initial adjacency matrix.
\d{Patchwork bootstrap}
uses the subgraph of nodes at most $n$ steps away from a random set of seed vertices (egonets);
for bootstrap estimates of the degree distribution, adjustments are needed for the degrees of the vertices 
and the time(s) at which they enter the patch (use each directed edge exactly once).
Check the \texttt{snowboot} package.

