Since linear combinations and products of Gaussian process kernels are still kernels,
a neural network, starting with primitive kernels and alternating those two operations, 
can be used to model them --
this replaces the automated statistician's discrete search on a context-free grammar with an end-to-end differentiable optimization problem.
