Illustrated introduction to Bayesian optimization followed by non-trivial examples: 
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Bayesian modeling of preferences 
\begin{align*}
  & P[ X \succ Y ] = \Phi\bigl( f(X) - f(Y) \bigr) \\
  & f \sim \text{GP}
\end{align*}
(the Bradley--Terry model assumes $f$ is linear and uses a logit instead of the probit $\Phi$);
\item Hierarchical reinforcement learning.
\end{compactitem}
