\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Texture networks: feed-forward synthesis\\ of textures and stylized images} \\
  D. Ulyanov et al (2016)
\end{book}
To generate a texture (target), find a CNN $f$ 
generating similar VGG features, 
\ie, minimizing 
\[ \n{ \text{VGG}\, f(\text{noise}) - \text{VGG}\,\text{target} }. \]
For style transfer, use
\[ \n{ \text{VGG}\, f(\text{noise}, \text{content}) - \text{VGG}\,\text{target} }, \]
where the target is fixed.


