\draw[->,thick] (D1) -- (E2);
\draw[->,thick] (D2) -- (E1);
\draw[->,thick] (D2) -- (E2);
\draw[->,thick] (E1) -- (F1);
\draw[->,thick] (E2) -- (F2);
\end{tikzpicture}
\]
Instead, cross-stitch units use two representations at each level, but blends them.
\[
\begin{tikzpicture}[
  >=stealth,yscale=.5,xscale=1,
