\begin{book}
  \emph{On the equivalence between quadrature rules and random features} \\
  F. Bach (2015)
\end{book}
The quadrature problem can be formulated as the problem of approximating 
an element $i : f \mapsto \int_D f$ of a Hilbert space 
as a linear combination of well-chosen elements $\text{ev}_x: f \mapsto f(x)$.

It is similar to the kernel approximation problem: 
finding a low-dimensional embedding $\phi$
such that $k(x,y) \approx \langle \phi(x), \phi(y) \rangle$.

