\]

A partition of $E$ is: 
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item A partition $\pi$ of $E$;
\item A set structure on each block of $\pi$; 
\item A set structure on $\pi$.
\end{compactitem}
This gives $\text{Partitions} = U(U-1)$, and 
$\text{Partitions}(x) = \exp( e^x - 1 )$ (Bell numbers).

A \emph{weighted species} is a functor
$\mathfrak{set} \to R\text{-}\mathfrak{set}$,
where $R = k((t_1,t_2,\dots))$
is a field of formal power series
and $R\text{-}\mathfrak{set}$ is 
the category of $R$-weighted finite sets.
An $R$-weighted finite set is a set $A$ 
with a map $w : A \to R$.
One associates power series associated 
to a weighted species as before, 
by replacing the size $\va A$
with the inventory $\va A _w = \sum_{a \in A} w(a)$.
The usual operations ($+$, $\cdot$, $\circ$, ${}'$, ${}^\bullet$, $\times$, $\square$) extend to weighted species. 
Weighted species can be used to compute, e.g.,
the number of rooted trees with a given number of nodes
and a given number of leaves.

A \emph{$k$-sort species} 
is a functor $\mathfrak{mset}(k) \to \mathfrak{set}$,
where $\mathfrak{mset}(k)$
is the category of multisets with $k$ sorts of elements (colours),
\ie, of $k$-tuples of sets.

