  W.H. Press and F.J. Dyson (2012)
\end{book}
In the iterated prisoner's dilemma (IPD), 
a longer (but still finite) memory
does not give any advantage (over a 1-period memory).
Strategies can be modeled by a Markov chain.
A player can decide on his/her opponent's rewards
(but not on his/her own).

