  K. He et al.
\end{book}
Rectified linear units (ReLU) $f(y) = y_+$
can be generalized to parametric
rectified linear units 
$f(y) = y_+ - a y_-$,
where $a$ is learned (and not penalized -- like biases).
The weights can be initialized randomly.
% by keeping track of the variance of the outputs.

