Using the FP-tree to extract frequent itemsets is trickier: 
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Start with the least frequent item;
\item If it is sufficiently frequent, consider the subtree it defines, 
  update the counts for the conditional FP-tree
  and discard the leaves (the item itself);
\item Process this conditional FP-tree recursively;
\item Discard the item and iterate with the next least frequent item, until the tree is empty.
\end{compactitem}

\nextbook
\begin{book}
  \emph{Efficient implementations of Apriori and Eclat}\\
  C. Borgelt (2003)
\end{book}
The frequent itemset (FIS) mining algorithms \emph{Apriori} and \emph{Eclat}
both explore the same prefix tree 
