%Hierarchical coordinate frames
%Recognizing objects: 3 approaches
%- Deep convolutional nets
%- Parts-based model
%- Features commonly-used in computer vision
%Problem with convolutional nets:
%- The position/orientation of the features is not kept (e.g., relative position of eyes, nose, mouth)
%- Translation-invariant, but not viewpoint-invariant
%
\d{Gaussian processes} can be used to optimize the hyper-parameters, in a Bayesian way:
%- Grid search
%- Random search
%- Use machine learning to find the best (better) parameters
they estimate a function 
\[ f: \text{hyperparameters} \longmapsto \text{quality of the result} \]
by providing an estimate and an error, \ie, $f(x) \sim N(\hat f(x), \sigma_x)$,
and one can evaluate the function at the hyperparameters with the biggest expected improvement
on the best values so far
\[ E[ \text{improvement} | \text{improvement} > 0 ]. \]

