\end{book}

People still use the \emph{1-factor gaussian copula}
\begin{align*}
  &\cor(X_i,X) = \rho \\
  &i \neq j \implies X_i | X \perp\!\!\!\perp X_j | X
\end{align*}
to price CDO tranches. 
The authors suggest a \emph{stochastic correlation model} with a
gaussian copula of the form
\begin{align*}
  &\cor(X_i,X) = \rho_i \\
  &i \neq j \implies X_i | X \perp\!\!\!\perp X_j | X \\
  &\rho_i \in \{0, \rho, 1\}
\end{align*}
where the $\rho_i$ are discrete random variables.

