\nextbook

\begin{book}
  \emph{Building a hedge fund portfolio\\ with kurtosis and skewness}\\
  M. Anson et al.\\
  Journal of alternative investments (2007)
\end{book}

\emph{Polynomial goal programming} (PGP) solves multi-objective
optimization problems as follows:
\begin{compactitem}[--]
\item Solve the problem for each objective separately; let
  $f_i^{\max}$ be the optimum of the $i$th objective $f_i$;
\item Minimize $\prod (1 + (f_i^{\max} - f_i)) ^ {\alpha_i}$ under the
  same constraints; the $\alpha_i$ are user-chosen parameters.
\end{compactitem}

The authors prefer PGP to a linear combination of the objectives --
the methods are actually equivalent, under a monotonic transformation
of the objective functions.

