\emph{Should owners of Nasdaq stocks\\ fear short-selling?}\\
S.E. Christophe et al.\\
Journal of portfolio management (spring 2007)
\end{book}

Short selling is not detrimental to stock returns: 
\begin{compactenum}[--]
\item only extreme short selling (over 10\%) has a negative impact on stock returns, but only 5 basis points per percentage point;
\item dealer short-selling has a positive impact on returns: market makers only short when they receive many buy orders.
\end{compactenum}

The article did not study the effect of short-selling on volatility or
during a crash.

