  F.J. Fabozzi et al.\\
  Journal of investing (2006)
\end{book}

The \emph{time diversification index} (TDI) is 
$$ \dfrac{
  \textrm{Short-term Sharpe Ratio}
}{
  \textrm{Long-term Sharpe ratio}
}
$$
where the (generalized) Sharpe ratio is 
$$
\textrm{Sharpe ratio} =
\dfrac{\textrm{Risk}}{\textrm{Expected returns}}
$$
for some measure of risk (standard deviation, value at risk, etc.)

